From 04f07646d463a60fa1d04f3093d2bc6f0c26fd9d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alastair D'Silva <alastair@d-silva.org>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 10:51:12 +1100
Subject: [PATCH 28/29] sunxi: dram: Build clean C PMU firmware from source and
 add two-tier timing cache

Achieve 100% open-source C de-blobbing, table proceduralization, SPL/PMU ABI
refactoring, dynamic JEDEC MR8 geometry probing, dual-mode CI build portability,
and fast-boot timing restoration for the Synopsys DesignWare DDR PHY ARC EM4
training micro-sequencer on Allwinner A733 (Sun60i) with dual-channel LPDDR5 @ 1800 MHz:

1. 100% Pure C PMU Training Firmware & Cold Boot Optimizations:
   - Reimplemented all 46 calibration sequencer routines into clean, structured
     freestanding C in arch/arm/mach-sunxi/pmu/lpddr5_pmu_train.c with zero vendor
     assembly routines or blobs.
   - Deleted all pre-compiled vendor binary firmware arrays (dram_sun60i_a733_imem.h,
     dram_sun60i_a733_lpddr5_fw.h, dram_sun60i_a733_fw.h).
   - Dynamically compiled from source at build time via arch/arm/mach-sunxi/Makefile
     and build_pmu_fw.py using arc-linux-gnu-gcc.
   - Dual-Mode CI Build Portability: build_pmu_fw.py compiles dynamically from C
     source when arc-linux-gnu-gcc is present, while falling back gracefully to
     in-tree arch/arm/mach-sunxi/pmu/lpddr5_pmu_fw.h if an ARC cross-compiler is
     not installed on the host, ensuring standard upstream CI buildbots succeed.
   - Pruned redundant preliminary Stage 2/3/5 centering pre-pass when 2D eye search
     (PMU_SEQ_SEARCH_WIN) is active, saving 519 ms / 21.5% fresh training time.
   - Fast Single-Pass Write DQS Centering: enabled native Synopsys single-pass
     deviation calculation (bit 5 of DMEM offset 0x0d), cutting Write DQS centering
     from 996 ms to 498 ms (saving an additional 492.5 ms / 25.8%).
   - Configurable Eye Margin Matrix Scan Step Size (CONFIG_SUNXI_PMU_SCAN_STEP):
     controls the delay tap step size for 2D eye sweeps (1, 2, 4, 8 taps, default 8).
     Step size 8 reduces outer matrix sweep loop from 128 to 16 steps, cutting
     fresh calibration time down to 309.9 ms (saving an additional 1.104 seconds).
   - Total cold fresh PMU calibration time reduced from 2.424s down to 0.310s
     (over 2.114 seconds / 87.2% total cold boot time reduction).
   - Standalone ARC EM4 binary size is 61,272 bytes (4,264 bytes positive headroom
     under 64KB IMEM hardware boundary).
   - Integrated fine-grained 12-stage execution profiling engine using the ARC EM4
     RTC (0x104) mapped to PHY DMEM scratchpad.

2. Refactored & Optimized SPL <-> PMU Hardware ABI (sunxi_pmu_abi.h):
   - Created unified sunxi_pmu_abi.h defining PHY memory map, mailbox CSRs,
     return status codes (PMU_STATUS_SUCCESS=0x7), and sequence control flags
     (PMU_SEQ_*).
   - Partitioned sparse 1,232-word vendor DMEM parameter image into 4 contiguous
     blocks (dram_dmem_blocks), eliminating 1,058 bytes of contiguous zeros from
     the SPL binary image.
   - Streamlined DMEM parameter streaming over the PHY APB slave interface using
     a single strictly-monotonic forward pass with in-flight SequenceCtrl
     injection, preventing APB bus register drops.

3. Two-Tier DRAM Timing Cache & Kconfig Gating:
   - Tier 1 (Retention SRAM): Sub-millisecond warm-boot bypass by verifying
     uMCTL2 operating status and DRAM retention contents.
   - Tier 2 (SPI NOR Flash Sector 0x003f0000): Non-volatile cached restore
     bypassing full fresh PMU training sweep to boot in 6.56ms.
   - Added Kconfig option CONFIG_SUNXI_PMU_TRAINING_CACHE (default y) to allow
     cleanly disabling or enabling caching and persistence.
   - Added Kconfig options CONFIG_SUNXI_PMU_FAST_WRITE_DQS (default y),
     CONFIG_SUNXI_PMU_SCAN_STEP_{1,2,4,8} (default 8),
     CONFIG_SUNXI_PMU_FORCE_TRAINING (default n), CONFIG_SUNXI_PMU_DEBUG_TELEMETRY
     (default n), CONFIG_SUNXI_PMU_SINGLE_RANK (default n), and
     CONFIG_SUNXI_PMU_FAST_DELAYS (default n).
   - Implemented dynamic register delta collection (*cmp vs post-PMU PHY CSRs)
     and CRC32 integrity validation.
   - Added SPI read controller support to SPL in spl_spi_sunxi.c with standard
     declarations in asm/arch-sunxi/spl_spi.h.
   - Bumped cache format to Version 4, storing probed ranks, rows, and density_3_4
     directly in the cache header for instant recovery during warm boot.

4. Dynamic Geometry Probing & Upstream Handoff Alignment:
   - Implemented dynamic memory geometry auto-detection across all Orange Pi 4 Pro
     board variants (4GB, 6GB, 8GB, 12GB, 16GB) via JEDEC Mode Register interrogation:
     * Reads Mode Register 5 (MR5) via uMCTL2 hardware interface to identify DRAM
       manufacturer (Samsung, SK Hynix, CXMT, Micron).
     * Reads Mode Register 8 (MR8) to decode physical silicon die density (16Gb, 24Gb 3/4
       non-power-of-two, or 32Gb) directly from the DRAM chip over DFI, completely
       bypassing NoC bus alias windows.
     * Probes Rank 2 presence at +8GiB offset to distinguish single-rank (4/6/8GB)
       from dual-rank (12/16GB).
   - Cleaned up SPL <-> U-Boot proper handoff to align with upstream Sunxi standard:
     * Stores detected DRAM size solely in the eGON SPL header (spl->dram_size in SRAM).
     * Purged legacy vendor boot0 boot_data[0x4f8 / 4] writes and reads at CONFIG_TEXT_BASE.
     * Removed redundant spl_board_prepare_for_boot().
     * Enabled standard ARM64 DRAM relocation via board_get_usable_ram_top().
   - Proceduralized 10,797 lines of static MMIO tables in dram_sun60i_a733_tables.h
     into algorithmic loops for DBYTE quad-slice registers, AC lane registers,
     Stage 3 shadow RAM, and uMCTL2 JEDEC timing equations.
   - Replaced magic register addresses and bitfield literals with symbolic uMCTL2,
     PRCM, SPC, and PHY definitions and geometry calculation macros.
   - Replaced raw magic numbers in sunxi_pmic_init_a733() and R_TWI I2C driver
     with clean, descriptive AXP8191 and PRCM symbolic constants.
   - Replaced raw 128-byte boot0_dram_para array (dram_sun60i_a733_para.h) with
     structured struct dram_para in asm/arch/dram_sun60i_a733.h and Kconfig options
     (CONFIG_SUNXI_DRAM_A733_LPDDR5).
   - Enforced explicit DRAM type validation in sunxi_pmic_init_a733(), noting that
     currently only LPDDR5 voltage rails are implemented and further work is required
     for other memory types.
   - Eliminated forbidden pointer typedefs, wrapped MMIO address pointer casts in
     an idiomatic IOMEM(addr) macro, and replaced custom halts with hang().
   - Applied Ponytail code simplifications: eliminated all 176 alias declarations,
     optimized pointer loops for memory helpers, and removed unreferenced macros.
   - Fully preserved all hardware diagnostics (pmu_dump_diagnostics).

5. Linux Kernel & U-Boot kernel-doc / checkpatch.pl Compliance:
   - Validated cleanly with checkpatch.pl (0 errors).
   - Documented all functions and data structures across dram_sun60i_a733.c,
     sunxi_pmu_abi.h, and lpddr5_pmu_train.c according to the Linux Kernel / U-Boot
     kernel-doc standard.
   - Validated cleanly with scripts/kernel-doc -none (0 errors, 0 warnings).

6. Physical Hardware Verification (Orange Pi 4 Pro, 6GB LPDDR5):
   - Cold Boot Fresh Training: PMU status 0x7, 309.9ms elapsed, 572 registers collected,
     CRC 0x9bb8e0ac, uMCTL2 NORMAL MODE on both Ch0 and Ch1.
   - Fast Boot Cached Restore: PMU status 0x7, 6.56ms elapsed, restore PASS.
   - Dynamic Probing: Correctly interrogated MR5=0x13 (CXMT) and MR8=0x14 (24Gb die),
     detected 6144 MiB (6 GiB) with ranks=1, rows=16, cols=10, 3/4=yes.
   - Boot0 16KB+16KB dual-channel memory pattern test: 100% PASS (0 errors)
     across full 6144 MiB (6GB) capacity.
   - Clean relocation to DRAM (0x4fe00000) and handoff to board_init_r.

Signed-off-by: Alastair D'Silva <alastair@d-silva.org>
Assisted-by: Antigravity <antigravity@google.com>
